============================================================================================
Part 2: TAIL piece -- CORRECTED exponent extraction.
g(K) itself grows only like ln(n) (Part 1's own printed g(K) column
already shows this: e.g. gamma=0.5, g(K) goes 16.9 -> 41.5 as n goes
1e3 -> 1e8, i.e. roughly LINEAR in ln(n), not in n). The quantity that
actually matters for the union bound is e^{g(K)} ~ n^lambda, where
lambda := d(g(K))/d(ln n), fitted here by least squares across ALL
sampled n (not a naive two-point power-law fit of g(K) itself against n,
which -- as an earlier version of this script mistakenly did --
silently underestimates the true exponent lambda by roughly the ratio
ln(ln n)/ln(n), giving a spuriously small 'mu' and an insufficient C.
Self-caught before any claim was made; corrected version below.
============================================================================================

